# English library: build log

Claude took the build over from Codex on 2026-10-25 at Alex's request ("好那你按照codex 需求来重建，然后开始充分的测试，一定要仔细的看结果以及评量"). The plan being executed is [english-library.md](english-library.md) (stages) with [plan.md](plan.md) (language compatibility contract) and [prompt-audit.md](prompt-audit.md) (candidate prompts). One row per measured step; mistakes stay in the log.

## Implementation decisions (what the plan left to the implementer)

| Decision | Choice | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Where legacy answers become canonical | At the three model boundaries that read an answer: `extraction.sift`, `matching.check`, `judging._record`; and at the consumers that compare stored values (`service` tier counts, the UI adapter's kind and tier maps). Storage readers return rows as written. | Stored requests of the Chinese configurations stay byte-identical (their builders print the stored values), so a cached replay of an old configuration still costs nothing; new writers store canonical values. |
| Which prompt version is English | Extraction version ≥ 6 (`role-v6`, `categories-v6`), `matching-v2`, `judging-v3`, `idea-v11`. The schema, the dynamic request text and the retry note follow the version. | The version is the one switch Config already owns; no environment flag. |
| Schema enums | English enums only in the new schemas; `direction` becomes an enum of the four canonical values in `matching-v2` (it was free text). | Code over prose: the schema refuses an unknown value before any check reads it. |
| Year text | `universe.canonical_year(object_id, text)` full-matches the accepted single-year forms (FY2027, FY 2027, fiscal 2027, fiscal year 2027, 2027财年, CY2026, calendar 2026, calendar year 2026, 2026自然年, bare 2026) and writes `FY2027` for a company whose fiscal year differs from the calendar, else `2026`; multi-year and unknown text stay as written and never resolve a waiting dependency. Applied when a view and a dependency are written. | The waiting-dependency join compares year text; two spellings of one year must join, two years must not. |
| Half-year filter | `QUARTERLY` gains the English revenue forms (H1/H2/1H/2H revenue or sales, first-half/second-half revenue, half-year revenue); an event scheduled in a half-year is not matched in either language. | Review finding 4: translation must not bypass the admission check. |
| Successor orientation | Numeric bounds first (`lo`/`hi` on both ladders), the prose parser (now with billion/million/trillion) only when a ladder has none. | Every rung of the English library carries bounds. |
| Score orientation in bundles | `bundle.view_bundle` carries `lo`/`hi`; the UI adapter orients a theme ladder from the bounds and falls back to the prose magnitudes only without them. | Review finding 2: 12 of 18 themes reversed without `condition_zh`. |
| Universe | New version `poc-2026-10-25-en1`: theme names in English, the Chinese names kept as aliases; `resolve` also matches aliases. | The extraction request prints the theme catalogue; the English request must not show Chinese names. |
| Preflight | The request parsers accept both header languages; part D checks each prompt file against the enum set of its version. | The $0 replay must cover English requests before the first paid English call. |

## Baseline before any change (2026-10-25, preflight on `keyed-2026-10-25/archive-T2.sqlite`, `items-window-tags2-2026-10-24.sqlite`, `views-2026-10-25-v15-T4c.sqlite`)

| Check | Result |
|---|---|
| B extraction answers | 315 answers; evidence 806 → 694 kept; candidates 152 → 122 kept; 958 judged, 142 dropped |
| C matching records | 155 judged, 2 refused (3 "evidence has no decision") |
| D enum values in prompts | 68 judged, 0 missing |
| E keyed views (T4c) | 40 open, 40 keyed, 0 duplicate keys, review pool 23 |
| Python suite | 227 passed (Codex, 10:00) |

The same preflight must give the same B, C and E numbers after the conversion; D grows with the new prompt files.

## Steps

| # | Step | Measured | Cost |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | English runtime: `vocabulary.py` (canonical values, legacy conversion at the three answer boundaries and the comparing readers), `extraction` v6 schema and request, `matching-v2` schema (direction now an enum) and request, `judging-v3` schema and request, canonical year at write, half-year filter in both languages, orientation from bounds, bounds in bundles and the UI adapter, universe `poc-2026-10-25-en1` (English theme names), `poc-v17.json`, preflight parsers for both languages | Preflight on the same inputs: B 958 judged / 142 dropped with the identical reason table, C 155 / 2 identical, E unchanged, D 93 judged / 0 missing (was 68: the five English prompt files). Python `tests/` 85 passed (was 74 + 11 new in `test_english.py`); UI 22 passed (19 + 3). Six scratch mutants caught (raw sift, raw matching, year stored as written, orientation without bounds, half-year filter without English, adapter without bounds); each needed one decisive test, the orientation test was rewritten once because the prose parser also answered its first version. `docs/check.py` OK. | $0 |
| 1a | Mistake: the first replacement of the tier comparison in `service.py` matched inside `piece['tier']` and left `piecvocabulary…`; caught by importing the module before the suite. Two test fixtures were written blind (the judging prompt was built after the first record; the service test lacked the processing row that dates rows) and corrected after reading the code they drive. | — | $0 |
| 1b | Test fixtures of `test_keyed_views.py` and `test_identity_repair.py` now speak the canonical vocabulary (49 literals); the writer-failure test runs on `poc-v17` because its scripted answers are canonical. Scripted legacy answers in `test_sequential_replay.py` stay Chinese: they simulate a Chinese configuration. | — | $0 |
| 2 | Fresh English extraction, 3 independent samples each (one archive per sample, `poc/data/english-2026-10-25/check/archive-{1,2,3}.sqlite`) on the Q4 FY2026 transcript (52 k chars) and the results press release (26 k chars), read in full (`fresh-check-1.txt`) | Transcript: 8 candidates and 8–9 evidence items in every sample, 0 dropped by the sift, 0 Chinese characters in generated text; the same eight questions each time (FY2027 total revenue, data-center revenue, gross margin, non-GAAP opex growth, tax rate; Rubin shipment event; H200 China licence event; 2026 top-five capex theme); fiscal periods right (FY2027 = 2026-02-01..2027-01-31, themes calendar 2026); due days right (2027-02-25 for FY2027 figures; the undated licence at fiscal year-end 2027-01-31); bounds form valid partitions in 24 of 24 ladders; tiers right (CFO statements party_statement, press-release actuals fact). Press release: 3 candidates (total revenue, Data Center revenue, tax rate) in 3 of 3, one ladder written bottom-up and turned round by code. 36/28/31 s and $0.066/0.054/0.053 per transcript call; 13–15 s and $0.03 per release call. | $0.26 |
| 2a | Observations to count on the seed run, not fixed by prompt growth: (i) the 2026 capex theme came as a two-rung threshold ladder ("below / at least $700 billion") in 2 of 3 transcript samples where the Chinese runs gave five ranges: the candidate role's "Use five rungs, or two for yes/no" is looser than role-v5's 「梯子五格（只有是或否的问题两格）」; made faithful ("only a yes/no question about an event has two; a numeric figure always gets five ranges") before the seed run; (ii) one prose/bound disagreement (tax-rate Neutral "at most 19%" with hi = 20; another sample wrote hi = 19.0000001 for the inclusive end): code evaluates on the bounds, the prose is display; (iii) scope spelling varies across samples (tax rate: "", "GAAP", "GAAP and non-GAAP"; opex growth: "" vs "non-GAAP operating expenses"): a model-written scope is wording, so identity goes to the model there (D155) and the seed run must show no duplicate key. | — | $0 |
| 2b | Mistake found by Codex's grouping-study tests: giving the universe English theme names changed the request text of the Chinese prompt versions, so their stored requests no longer replayed byte-identically (`Prefix request differs`). The universe now keeps `legacy_name` for the Chinese builders; `name` is English. | — | $0 |
| 3 | Seed build launched (poc-v17, the 20 NVIDIA documents 2026-02-25..07-23, `--only NVDA --cap 5`, ledger `poc/data/english-2026-10-25/views.sqlite`), then stopped after 5 calls: the same grouping-study replay showed the first version of the year rule respelling a bare "2026" on an NVDA event as "FY2026" (NVDA's FY2026 ended in January 2026, so the text was wrong, and a stored Chinese request no longer replayed). Rule corrected: a fiscal form becomes FY2027 (or 2027 for a December year-end), a calendar form 2026, a bare year keeps its digits and is never reinterpreted; the period of a company's bare year is still its fiscal year (unchanged 06-views rule). The partial ledger is set aside in `aborted-1/`, the archive kept as cache. `tests/` + grouping study: 228 passed. Relaunched. | 5 calls | $0.12 |
| 3a | Mistake: the relaunch opened a fresh `views.sqlite` beside the aborted run's hot `views.sqlite-journal`; SQLite may roll a stale journal into a new file, so that ledger was set aside too (`aborted-2/`, its content looked right) and the build relaunched on a clean directory. Rule for the memory: never start a ledger next to a `*.sqlite-journal`. | 2 calls | $0.05 |
| 4 | Seed build finished: 20 documents 2026-02-25..07-23, all 20 routed and extracted, 0 failures (`run-seed.out`, `review-seed.txt`, trace `poc/reports/2026-10-25-english/trace-seed/`) | 12 theses (Chinese T2d on the same documents: 11), 65 evidence kept of 71 produced, 51 stored, 14 candidates → 13 kept → 12 theses + 1 merge (the 10-K's total-revenue candidate merged into v1 by the model), 23 judgements, 0 refusals, 0 schema refusals. `review_english_run.py`: 0 breaches: every kind, tier, push and label canonical, 0 Chinese characters in generated text, every year canonical, 0 duplicate keys, review pool 0. Trace diagnoses: 10 正常, 10 空手 (the routine 8-K bodies and the June note offering's underwriting agreement, indenture and legal opinion gave nothing, as in the Chinese runs). Drops: 5 "quote not in item" (paraphrased quotes), 1 link to a dropped candidate, 1 candidate without surviving evidence. Judgements read as an analyst's: opex growth moved Neutral → Bearish on 05-20 when guidance went from "low 40s" to "upper forties"; the tax-rate views followed the 16–18% revision. Request size on the same documents: English input tokens 5–10% below Chinese (8-K 3,622 vs 3,965; CFO commentary 7,630 vs 7,980), characters higher; cost per document the same. | 48 calls (20 extract, 12 match, 23 judge; 3 days judged) | $0.90 |
| 4a | Observations to carry into the week: (i) two tax-rate theses (v5 non-GAAP from the transcript, v8 GAAP from the release) for one guided number, kept apart by the basis rule; the transcript's quote reads "7% to 19%" where the release says 17.0–19.0%, so v5's Neutral band is 10–19%: a source transcription artefact plus the basis split; (ii) 0 dependencies were written in 12 new theses (the matching prompt asks for them; the model named none); (iii) the 2026 hyperscaler-capex theme opened with five ranges this time. | — | — |
| 5 | Idea route on the English seed ledger (`idea-v11`, poc-v17; new index `search-index.sqlite`, 15 views embedded for 1,893 tokens; `idea_english_probe.py`): four English ideas as of 2026-07-23 | 0 language slips in 8 calls; 5.7–8.2 s and $0.004–0.008 per idea. "NVIDIA will top $300 billion of data center revenue in FY2027": direct view v2, claim ≥ $300 billion evaluated on the bounds against the judged Bullish band ($300–350 billion) → holds; drivers v11 (hyperscaler capex) and v6 (Rubin shipments). "Hyperscaler capex peaks in 2026 and gross margins come under pressure": v11 and v3 direct, revenue views as drivers, the summary says the library judges the margin bullish, contrary to the idea. "Rubin production slips into 2027": v6 direct ("Yes"), the summary says the library does not support the slip. "H200 sales to China are coming back": v7 direct ("No" as judged), export-controls part reported as uncovered. Related views from the dependency graph: none, because the seed ledger holds no dependencies (observation 4a ii). | 8 idea calls + embeddings | $0.03 |
| 6 | Week 2026-07-24..31 launched on the same ledger, every object, cap $8 (`run-week.out`) | — | running |
